{"parentUuid":"0220b013-ae29-49d0-8996-16f01aad0263","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/harborlight","sessionId":"insight-13","version":"2.0.21","gitBranch":"fix/events-stream","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_01pbrkJqAZ2HeYRJjo6XoK4d","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Through nginx nothing arrived in 12 seconds; straight from the api container on 10.0.2.14 the events arrive every few seconds. So the app streams fine and nginx holds the response back. Let me read the site config."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":665,"output_tokens":69}},"uuid":"5878e7db-9836-498d-89fb-7d7e873aaba7","timestamp":"2026-09-23T11:14:19.000Z","requestId":"req_011CdrYy9UXrglTX7Ekn9Asa"}
{"parentUuid":"5878e7db-9836-498d-89fb-7d7e873aaba7","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/harborlight","sessionId":"insight-13","version":"2.0.21","gitBranch":"fix/events-stream","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_01eSOd8Xv03T3dkrYIzuNk7U","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01faUbhl8XRHj6sUbMbx17IV","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/dev/harborlight/deploy/nginx/harborlight.conf"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","usage":{"input_tokens":690,"output_tokens":127}},"uuid":"2221f18f-07ac-4760-b755-40e019e17a7d","timestamp":"2026-09-23T11:14:22.000Z","requestId":"req_011CLpbUlaPTR852MB3nwrle"}
{"parentUuid":"2221f18f-07ac-4760-b755-40e019e17a7d","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/harborlight","sessionId":"insight-13","version":"2.0.21","gitBranch":"fix/events-stream","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_01faUbhl8XRHj6sUbMbx17IV","content":"     1\tupstream hbl_api {\n     2\t    server 10.0.2.14:3000;\n     3\t    server 10.0.2.15:3000;\n     4\t}\n     5\t\n     6\tserver {\n     7\t    listen 443 ssl http2;\n     8\t    server_name staging.harborlight.example;\n     9\t\n    10\t    location / {\n    11\t        proxy_pass http://hbl_api;\n    12\t        proxy_set_header Host $host;\n    13\t        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;\n    14\t    }\n    15\t}"}]},"uuid":"ba7d8f68-0cbe-45a7-a87e-b71d2515cad4","timestamp":"2026-09-23T11:14:26.000Z"}
{"parentUuid":"ba7d8f68-0cbe-45a7-a87e-b71d2515cad4","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/harborlight","sessionId":"insight-13","version":"2.0.21","gitBranch":"fix/events-stream","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_01z7m4PfWqRA1MhxQfrYoSKz","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That's the cause. nginx buffers proxied responses by default (proxy_buffering is on): it reads the upstream response into its buffers and passes it on when a buffer fills or the response ends. For a normal API response that is invisible, but a server-sent events stream writes a few small lines at a time, so they sit in nginx's buffer until it has collected enough, which is the minute of silence and then the burst.\n\nThere are two ways to turn it off for this stream only: a location /v1/events block with proxy_buffering off, or the app sends the response header X-Accel-Buffering: no, which nginx honours per response. The header keeps the fix next to the code that needs it and works behind any nginx we put in front, so I'd do that. The heartbeat every 15 s already keeps the connection inside nginx's default 60 s read timeout, so nothing else has to change."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":776,"output_tokens":481}},"uuid":"e3c741dd-167c-411a-a34b-bc4f11f08c22","timestamp":"2026-09-23T11:14:34.000Z","requestId":"req_011CGrcc1vrPVubaYhsvuj3m"}
